            <div xml:id="d499">

                <pb facs="0698" n="608" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg608"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72112/5055: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-10-11T16:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 11,
                                1917—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 11—3:45
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>My despatch no. 4822, September 25 Admiralty Marshal states: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I understand from the Procurator General who has forwarded me letter
                            from Blockade Minister that when American Government approaches British
                            Government concerning the release of seizures involving American
                            interests to American citizens British Government <pb facs="0699"
                                n="609" xml:id="pg609"/> will be prepared to give same advantages as
                            heretofore afforded other Allied Governments”.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
